STORIES_LOAD("act",{"ac1":{"passage":[[1,3,11],[1,23,26]],"intro":[{"sc":"ascension","n":"After His suffering, Jesus showed Himself alive to His followers for forty days, with many convincing proofs, and spoke about the kingdom of God."},{"sc":"ascension","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Don't leave Jerusalem, but wait for the gift My Father promised. In a few days you will be baptised with the Holy Spirit."},{"sc":"ascension","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"You will receive power when the Holy Spirit comes on you; and you will be My witnesses in Jerusalem, and in all Judea and Samaria, and to the ends of the earth."},{"sc":"ascension","n":"After He said this, He was taken up before their very eyes, and a cloud hid Him from their sight. Two men dressed in white stood beside them: \"Why do you stand here looking into the sky? This same Jesus will come back in the same way you have seen Him go!\""},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"They went back to Jerusalem and gathered in the upstairs room, about 120 of them, praying together constantly, including Mary the mother of Jesus and His brothers. They chose Matthias, by casting lots, to replace Judas as one of the twelve."},{"sc":"ascension","n":"🔎 Did you know? Acts 1:8 is like a map of the whole book: Jerusalem (chapters 1 to 7), Judea and Samaria (chapters 8 to 12), and the ends of the earth (chapters 13 to 28). Watch the good news spread outward like ripples in a pond!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Wait, then go","text":"Jesus gave His followers a huge mission: to the ends of the earth! But first: wait and pray for the Holy Spirit's power. They couldn't do it in their own strength, and neither can we. Leaders pray together and depend on God's Spirit before they go."},"order":["Jesus appears for forty days","\"Wait for the gift My Father promised\"","\"You will be My witnesses\"","Jesus is taken up into a cloud","\"He will come back the same way\"","120 believers pray together"],"quiz":[{"q":"Where did Jesus say His followers would be witnesses?","o":["Jerusalem, Judea, Samaria and the ends of the earth","Only Jerusalem","Only Rome","Nowhere"],"why":"Acts 1:8."},{"q":"How long did Jesus appear after rising?","o":["Forty days","Three days","A year","Seven days"],"why":"Acts 1:3."},{"q":"Who replaced Judas?","o":["Matthias","Paul","Barnabas","Stephen"],"why":"Acts 1:26."}],"words":["WITNESSES","POWER","SPIRIT","WAIT","CLOUD","EARTH"]},"ac2":{"passage":[[2,1,13]],"intro":[{"sc":"upperroom","n":"When the day of Pentecost came, a harvest festival fifty days after Passover, the believers were all together in one place."},{"sc":"pentecost","n":"Suddenly a sound like the blowing of a violent wind came from heaven and filled the whole house!"},{"sc":"pentecost","n":"They saw what seemed to be tongues of fire that separated and came to rest on each of them. All of them were filled with the Holy Spirit and began to speak in other languages as the Spirit enabled them."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"Jerusalem was full of visitors from every nation for the festival. When they heard the sound, a crowd gathered, amazed, because each one heard them speaking in their own language!"},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"\"Aren't all these men from Galilee? How is it that each of us hears them in our own native language? People from Persia, Mesopotamia, Asia, Egypt and the parts of Libya near Cyrene, Rome, Crete and Arabia: we hear them declaring the wonders of God in our own tongues!\""},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"Some made fun of them: \"They've had too much wine!\""},{"sc":"pentecost","n":"🔎 Did you know? At the Tower of Babel (Genesis 11), God confused people's languages and scattered them. At Pentecost, God's Spirit brought people from many nations together, each hearing about Jesus in their own language! Africans from Egypt and Libya were there on the very first day."}],"lesson":{"title":"The Spirit speaks every language","text":"When the Holy Spirit came, the very first thing He did was let people hear about God in their own languages. God wants every nation to hear about Jesus in their mother tongue, including Yoruba, Hausa, Igbo, and every language in Africa. Leaders help others hear the good news in a way they understand."},"order":["The believers are together at Pentecost","A sound like a violent wind","Tongues of fire rest on each one","They speak in other languages","Visitors from every nation hear","Some say they're drunk"],"quiz":[{"q":"What appeared on each believer?","o":["Tongues of fire","Crowns","Doves","Clouds"],"why":"Acts 2:3."},{"q":"What could the visitors hear?","o":["God's wonders in their own languages","Nothing","Only Greek","Music"],"why":"Acts 2:8, 11."},{"q":"Which African places were mentioned?","o":["Egypt and Libya near Cyrene","Ethiopia and Sudan","Nigeria and Ghana","None"],"why":"Acts 2:10."}],"words":["PENTECOST","FIRE","WIND","SPIRIT","LANGUAGES","NATIONS"]},"ac3":{"passage":[[2,14,17],[2,22,24],[2,36,47]],"intro":[{"sc":"jerusalem","w":"bpeter","e":"stern","t":"Fellow Jews and all who live in Jerusalem, listen carefully! These people aren't drunk; it's only nine in the morning! No, this is what was spoken by the prophet Joel: 'In the last days, God says, I will pour out My Spirit on all people.'"},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"This was Peter, the same Peter who had denied Jesus three times, standing up boldly in front of thousands!"},{"sc":"jerusalem","w":"bpeter","e":"stern","t":"Jesus of Nazareth was handed over to you, and you put Him to death by nailing Him to the cross. But God raised Him from the dead! God has made this Jesus, whom you crucified, both Lord and Messiah."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"The people were cut to the heart. \"Brothers, what shall we do?\""},{"sc":"jerusalem","w":"bpeter","e":"smile","t":"Repent and be baptised, every one of you, in the name of Jesus Christ for the forgiveness of your sins. And you will receive the gift of the Holy Spirit. The promise is for you and your children!"},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"About three thousand people believed and were baptised that day!"},{"sc":"hut","n":"The believers devoted themselves to the apostles' teaching, to fellowship, to breaking bread and to prayer. They shared everything they had, sold possessions to give to anyone in need, met together every day, ate together with glad and sincere hearts, and praised God. And the Lord added to their number daily those who were being saved."}],"lesson":{"title":"A family that shares","text":"From scared Peter to a preacher of thousands! And the very first church was a family: learning together, eating together, praying together and sharing so nobody went without. Leaders build communities where people learn, pray, eat and share together."},"order":["Peter stands up to explain","\"This is what Joel spoke about\"","\"God raised Jesus from the dead\"","\"What shall we do?\"","Three thousand are baptised","The believers share everything"],"quiz":[{"q":"Which prophet did Peter quote?","o":["Joel","Isaiah","Jonah","Malachi"],"why":"Acts 2:16."},{"q":"How many people believed that day?","o":["About three thousand","Twelve","Five thousand","One hundred"],"why":"Acts 2:41."},{"q":"What four things did the first believers devote themselves to?","o":["Teaching, fellowship, breaking bread and prayer","Fishing, farming, building and selling","Singing only","Nothing"],"why":"Acts 2:42."}],"words":["PETER","SERMON","BAPTISED","THOUSAND","FELLOWSHIP","SHARE"]},"ac4":{"passage":[[3,1,10]],"intro":[{"sc":"temple","n":"One afternoon, Peter and John were going up to the temple at the time of prayer, three in the afternoon."},{"sc":"temple","n":"A man who had been lame from birth was being carried to the temple gate called Beautiful, where he was put every day to beg from people going in. He had never walked in his life; he was over forty years old."},{"sc":"temple","n":"When he saw Peter and John about to enter, he asked them for money."},{"sc":"temple","w":"bpeter","e":"stern","t":"Look at us!"},{"sc":"temple","n":"The man gave them his attention, expecting to get something from them."},{"sc":"temple","w":"bpeter","e":"smile","t":"Silver or gold I do not have, but what I do have I give you. In the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, walk!"},{"sc":"temple","n":"Peter took him by the right hand and helped him up. Instantly the man's feet and ankles became strong! He jumped to his feet and began to walk. Then he went with them into the temple courts, walking and jumping and praising God!"},{"sc":"temple","n":"When all the people saw him walking and praising God, and recognised him as the man who used to sit begging at the Beautiful gate, they were filled with wonder and amazement."}],"lesson":{"title":"Give what you have","text":"Peter didn't have money. But he had something better: the name and power of Jesus. Sometimes we think we can't help because we lack money or skills. Give what you DO have: your time, kindness, prayer, and Jesus. Leaders look people in the eye and offer what they truly have."},"order":["Peter and John go to the temple","A man lame from birth begs at the gate","He asks for money","\"Look at us!\"","\"Silver or gold I do not have\"","He walks, jumps and praises God"],"quiz":[{"q":"What was the temple gate called?","o":["Beautiful","Golden","Sheep Gate","Fish Gate"],"why":"Acts 3:2."},{"q":"What did Peter say he didn't have?","o":["Silver or gold","Faith","Time","Bread"],"why":"Acts 3:6."},{"q":"What did the man do after being healed?","o":["Walked, jumped and praised God","Ran home","Sat down again","Asked for money"],"why":"Acts 3:8."}],"words":["SILVER","GOLD","BEAUTIFUL","GATE","WALK","JUMP"]},"ac5":{"passage":[[4,1,4],[4,13,21]],"intro":[{"sc":"temple","n":"The temple leaders were furious that Peter and John were teaching that Jesus had risen from the dead. They arrested them and put them in jail overnight. But many who heard the message believed: about five thousand men!"},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"The next day, the rulers, elders and teachers met, including the high priest. They had Peter and John brought before them: \"By what power or what name did you do this?\""},{"sc":"praetorium","w":"bpeter","e":"stern","t":"It is by the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, whom you crucified but whom God raised from the dead, that this man stands before you healed. Salvation is found in no one else."},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"When they saw the courage of Peter and John and realised they were unschooled, ordinary men, they were astonished, and they took note that these men had been with Jesus."},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"They ordered them not to speak or teach at all in the name of Jesus."},{"sc":"praetorium","w":"bjohnapos","e":"stern","t":"Which is right in God's eyes: to listen to you, or to Him? You be the judges! As for us, we cannot help speaking about what we have seen and heard!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Courage from being with Jesus","text":"The religious leaders were puzzled: these were 'unschooled, ordinary men', fishermen! Where did their boldness come from? Then they realised: 'these men had been with Jesus'. Time with Jesus makes ordinary people brave. Leaders spend time with Jesus, and it shows."},"order":["Peter and John are arrested","Five thousand men believe","They stand before the council","\"By the name of Jesus\"","\"They had been with Jesus\"","\"We cannot stop speaking\""],"quiz":[{"q":"How did the council describe Peter and John?","o":["Unschooled, ordinary men","Rich priests","Soldiers","Kings"],"why":"Acts 4:13."},{"q":"What did the council notice about them?","o":["They had been with Jesus","They were tired","They were rich","They were scared"],"why":"Acts 4:13."},{"q":"What did Peter and John say they couldn't stop doing?","o":["Speaking about what they'd seen and heard","Fishing","Eating","Running"],"why":"Acts 4:20."}],"words":["COURAGE","ORDINARY","COUNCIL","BOLD","NAME","WITH"]},"ac6":{"passage":[[4,32,37],[5,1,11]],"intro":[{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"All the believers were one in heart and mind. No one claimed that any of their possessions was their own; they shared everything. And there were no needy people among them!"},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"Joseph, a Levite from Cyprus, whom the apostles called Barnabas, which means 'son of encouragement', sold a field he owned, and brought the money and put it at the apostles' feet."},{"sc":"jerusalem","w":"bbarnabas","e":"smile","t":"This is for anyone who needs it."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"But a man named Ananias and his wife Sapphira also sold some property. They kept back part of the money for themselves, but brought the rest and pretended it was the full price, so they'd look as generous as Barnabas."},{"sc":"jerusalem","w":"bpeter","e":"stern","t":"Ananias, why have you lied to the Holy Spirit? The land was yours, and the money was yours to do with as you wished. You haven't lied just to people, but to God."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"When Ananias heard this, he fell down and died. Three hours later, Sapphira came in, told the same lie, and the same thing happened to her. Great fear seized the whole church."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"🔎 Did you know? Ananias and Sapphira weren't punished for keeping some money; Peter said it was theirs to keep. They were punished for lying to God, pretending to be more generous than they were, at the very start of the church, when honesty mattered so much."}],"lesson":{"title":"Real generosity, no pretending","text":"Barnabas gave generously and simply. Ananias and Sapphira wanted the praise without the cost, so they lied. God cares more about honesty than about the size of our gift. Leaders give honestly, and never pretend to be more generous or holy than they are."},"order":["The believers share everything","Barnabas sells a field and gives the money","His name means 'son of encouragement'","Ananias and Sapphira keep back some money","They pretend it's the full price","They lied to God, not just people"],"quiz":[{"q":"What does Barnabas mean?","o":["Son of encouragement","Son of thunder","Rock","Gift of God"],"why":"Acts 4:36."},{"q":"What did Ananias and Sapphira do wrong?","o":["They lied about how much they gave","They kept their money","They sold land","They gave too much"],"why":"Acts 5:2-4."},{"q":"Who did Peter say they had lied to?","o":["The Holy Spirit, God","Only Peter","Only the church","Nobody"],"why":"Acts 5:3-4."}],"words":["BARNABAS","ENCOURAGE","SHARE","HONEST","GENEROUS","LIE"]},"ac7":{"passage":[[6,1,7]],"intro":[{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"As the church grew, a problem arose. The Greek-speaking believers complained that their widows were being overlooked in the daily distribution of food. The Hebrew-speaking widows were getting fed; the others weren't!"},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"The twelve apostles gathered all the believers together."},{"sc":"jerusalem","w":"bpeter","e":"smile","t":"It wouldn't be right for us to neglect the ministry of God's word to wait on tables. Brothers and sisters, choose seven men from among you who are known to be full of the Spirit and wisdom. We will put them in charge of this, and we'll give our attention to prayer and the ministry of the word."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"This pleased the whole group. They chose seven, including Stephen, a man full of faith and the Holy Spirit, and Philip. Interestingly, all seven had Greek names: they chose people from the very group that had been left out!"},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"The apostles prayed and laid their hands on them. So the word of God spread, and the number of disciples in Jerusalem increased rapidly."}],"lesson":{"title":"Solve problems fairly, share the load","text":"When some widows were being left out, the leaders didn't ignore it or get defensive. They listened, shared the work, and gave responsibility to people of good character, from the very group that had been overlooked. Leaders fix unfairness quickly, and delegate wisely."},"order":["The church grows","Greek-speaking widows are overlooked","The apostles gather everyone","\"Choose seven full of the Spirit and wisdom\"","They choose Stephen, Philip and five others","The word of God spreads"],"quiz":[{"q":"What was the problem?","o":["Some widows were overlooked in the food sharing","There was no food","People were fighting","The temple was closed"],"why":"Acts 6:1."},{"q":"What qualities did the seven need?","o":["Full of the Spirit and wisdom","Rich and strong","Tall and loud","Old and famous"],"why":"Acts 6:3."},{"q":"Which famous person was one of the seven?","o":["Stephen","Paul","Peter","Barnabas"],"why":"Acts 6:5."}],"words":["SEVEN","WIDOWS","FAIR","SERVE","WISDOM","DELEGATE"]},"ac8":{"passage":[[6,8,15],[7,54,60]],"intro":[{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"Stephen, full of God's grace and power, performed great wonders among the people. Some men began to argue with him, but they could not stand up against his wisdom and the Spirit by whom he spoke."},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"So they secretly paid men to lie about him, and dragged him before the council. All who were sitting in the council looked at Stephen, and saw that his face was like the face of an angel."},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"Stephen gave a long speech telling the whole story of Israel, from Abraham to Moses to David, and showed how they had always resisted God's messengers. The leaders were furious."},{"sc":"throneglory","w":"bstephen","e":"big","t":"Look! I see heaven open and the Son of Man standing at the right hand of God!"},{"sc":"citygate","n":"At this they covered their ears, yelled, and rushed at him. They dragged him out of the city and began to stone him. The witnesses laid their coats at the feet of a young man named Saul."},{"sc":"citygate","w":"bstephen","e":"worried","t":"Lord Jesus, receive my spirit. Lord, do not hold this sin against them."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"When he had said this, he fell asleep. And Saul approved of his killing."},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"🔎 Did you know? Jesus usually 'sits' at God's right hand. But Stephen saw Him STANDING, as if rising to welcome His faithful servant home. And Stephen's prayer, 'Do not hold this sin against them', echoes Jesus' 'Father, forgive them.'"}],"lesson":{"title":"Forgive like Jesus","text":"Stephen was the first Christian to die for his faith. Even as stones flew, he saw Jesus standing to welcome him, and prayed for his killers, just as Jesus had. And watching was a young man named Saul. Stephen's forgiveness may have planted a seed in Saul's heart. Leaders forgive, even when it costs everything."},"order":["Stephen does great wonders","False witnesses accuse him","His face shines like an angel's","\"I see the Son of Man standing!\"","They stone him; Saul watches","\"Lord, do not hold this sin against them\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Stephen's face look like?","o":["The face of an angel","Angry","Scared","Tired"],"why":"Acts 6:15."},{"q":"What did Stephen see in heaven?","o":["Jesus standing at God's right hand","A golden city","Angels singing","Moses"],"why":"Acts 7:56."},{"q":"Who watched the coats while Stephen was stoned?","o":["A young man named Saul","Peter","Barnabas","Philip"],"why":"Acts 7:58."}],"words":["STEPHEN","SHINING","FORGIVE","STANDING","MARTYR","SAUL"]},"ac9":{"passage":[[8,26,40]],"intro":[{"sc":"wilderness","n":"After Stephen's death, the believers scattered, and Philip went to Samaria and preached about Jesus there. Many believed. Then an angel of the Lord said to Philip: \"Go south to the desert road that goes down from Jerusalem to Gaza.\""},{"sc":"chariot","n":"So he started out, and on his way he met an Ethiopian official, an important man in charge of all the treasury of the Kandake, the queen of the Ethiopians. He had gone to Jerusalem to worship, and on his way home was sitting in his chariot, reading the book of Isaiah the prophet aloud."},{"sc":"chariot","n":"The Spirit told Philip, \"Go to that chariot and stay near it.\" So Philip ran up to the chariot!"},{"sc":"chariot","w":"bphilipev","e":"smile","t":"Do you understand what you are reading?"},{"sc":"chariot","w":"beunuch","e":"worried","t":"How can I, unless someone explains it to me? Come up and sit with me. Tell me: is the prophet talking about himself, or someone else? 'He was led like a sheep to the slaughter...'"},{"sc":"chariot","n":"Then Philip began with that very passage of Scripture, Isaiah 53, and told him the good news about Jesus."},{"sc":"jordan","w":"beunuch","e":"big","t":"Look, here is water! What can stop me from being baptised?"},{"sc":"jordan","n":"They both went down into the water, and Philip baptised him. When they came up out of the water, the Spirit suddenly took Philip away, and the Ethiopian went on his way rejoicing, all the way home to Africa!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Be ready to explain","text":"The Ethiopian had the Bible but didn't understand it. Philip obeyed a strange instruction, ran to the chariot, and asked a simple question: 'Do you understand?' Then he explained it, starting where the man was. Leaders are ready to help others understand God's word. And the good news reached Africa very early!"},"order":["An angel sends Philip to a desert road","An Ethiopian official reads Isaiah in his chariot","Philip runs up to the chariot","\"Do you understand what you're reading?\"","Philip explains it's about Jesus","The Ethiopian is baptised and goes home rejoicing"],"quiz":[{"q":"What was the Ethiopian reading?","o":["Isaiah","Genesis","Psalms","Daniel"],"why":"Acts 8:28."},{"q":"What was his job?","o":["In charge of the queen of Ethiopia's treasury","A soldier","A farmer","A priest"],"why":"Acts 8:27."},{"q":"What did Philip do when the Spirit told him to go to the chariot?","o":["Ran up to it","Walked slowly","Ignored it","Hid"],"why":"Acts 8:30."}],"words":["ETHIOPIA","CHARIOT","ISAIAH","PHILIP","BAPTISED","AFRICA"]},"ac10":{"passage":[[9,1,9]],"intro":[{"sc":"praetorium","n":"Meanwhile, Saul was still breathing out murderous threats against the Lord's disciples. He went to the high priest and asked for letters to the synagogues in Damascus, so he could arrest any followers of 'the Way', men or women, and take them as prisoners to Jerusalem."},{"sc":"damascus","n":"As he neared Damascus on his journey, suddenly a light from heaven flashed around him, brighter than the midday sun! He fell to the ground and heard a voice:"},{"sc":"damascus","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"Saul, Saul, why do you persecute Me?"},{"sc":"damascus","w":"bsaul","e":"shock","t":"Who are You, Lord?"},{"sc":"damascus","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"I am Jesus, whom you are persecuting. Now get up and go into the city, and you will be told what you must do."},{"sc":"damascus","n":"The men travelling with Saul stood there speechless; they heard the sound but didn't see anyone. Saul got up from the ground, but when he opened his eyes, he could see nothing."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"So they led him by the hand into Damascus. For three days he was blind, and didn't eat or drink anything."},{"sc":"damascus","n":"🔎 Did you know? Notice Jesus didn't say 'Why are you persecuting My followers?' but 'Why are you persecuting ME?' When someone hurts a Christian, Jesus takes it personally."}],"lesson":{"title":"No one is too far for Jesus","text":"Saul was the most dangerous enemy of the church, on his way to arrest Christians. Jesus stopped him in his tracks, not to destroy him, but to change him. Pray for people who seem furthest from God; Jesus can turn the worst enemy into the greatest friend."},"order":["Saul threatens the disciples","He heads to Damascus to arrest them","A light from heaven flashes","\"Saul, Saul, why do you persecute Me?\"","\"I am Jesus\"","Saul is blind for three days"],"quiz":[{"q":"Where was Saul going?","o":["Damascus","Rome","Egypt","Bethlehem"],"why":"Acts 9:3."},{"q":"What did the voice say?","o":["Saul, Saul, why do you persecute Me?","Go home","You're forgiven","Run!"],"why":"Acts 9:4."},{"q":"How long was Saul blind?","o":["Three days","One hour","Forty days","A year"],"why":"Acts 9:9."}],"words":["SAUL","DAMASCUS","LIGHT","BLIND","VOICE","CHANGED"]},"ac11":{"passage":[[9,10,20],[9,23,25]],"intro":[{"sc":"townnight","n":"In Damascus there was a disciple named Ananias. The Lord called to him in a vision: \"Ananias! Go to the house of Judas on Straight Street and ask for a man from Tarsus named Saul, for he is praying.\""},{"sc":"townnight","w":"bananiasd","e":"worried","t":"Lord, I've heard many reports about this man and all the harm he has done to Your people in Jerusalem! And he has come here with authority to arrest everyone who calls on Your name!"},{"sc":"townnight","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Go! This man is My chosen instrument to proclaim My name to the Gentiles and their kings, and to the people of Israel."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"So Ananias went. He placed his hands on Saul."},{"sc":"townnight","w":"bananiasd","e":"smile","t":"Brother Saul, the Lord Jesus, who appeared to you on the road, has sent me so that you may see again and be filled with the Holy Spirit."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Immediately, something like scales fell from Saul's eyes, and he could see again! He got up and was baptised. And at once he began to preach in the synagogues that Jesus is the Son of God!"},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Soon the Jewish leaders plotted to kill Saul. They watched the city gates day and night. But his followers took him by night and lowered him in a basket through an opening in the city wall!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Courage to welcome an enemy","text":"Ananias was terrified, and honest with God about it. But he obeyed. And his first words to the man who'd come to arrest him were: 'Brother Saul'. Ananias is barely mentioned in the Bible, but he helped launch the greatest missionary in history. Leaders obey even when afraid, and welcome changed enemies as family."},"order":["The Lord calls Ananias in a vision","\"Go to Saul\"","Ananias is afraid","\"He is My chosen instrument\"","\"Brother Saul\"","Scales fall from Saul's eyes"],"quiz":[{"q":"Why was Ananias afraid?","o":["Saul had harmed and arrested believers","He was sick","He was lost","He was poor"],"why":"Acts 9:13-14."},{"q":"What did Ananias call Saul?","o":["Brother Saul","Enemy","Sir","Stranger"],"why":"Acts 9:17."},{"q":"How did Saul escape from Damascus?","o":["Lowered in a basket through the wall","On a horse","By boat","Through the gate"],"why":"Acts 9:25."}],"words":["ANANIAS","BROTHER","SCALES","BASKET","AFRAID","OBEYED"]},"ac12":{"passage":[[9,26,31]],"intro":[{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"When Saul came to Jerusalem, he tried to join the disciples. But they were all afraid of him!"},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"They didn't believe he had really become a disciple. Maybe it was a trick to get inside and arrest them all."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"But Barnabas took him and brought him to the apostles."},{"sc":"jerusalem","w":"bbarnabas","e":"smile","t":"Listen, everyone. Saul saw the Lord on the road, and the Lord spoke to him. And in Damascus he preached fearlessly in the name of Jesus. I believe him."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"So Saul stayed with them and moved about freely in Jerusalem, speaking boldly in the name of the Lord."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"Then the church throughout Judea, Galilee and Samaria enjoyed a time of peace and was strengthened. Living in the fear of the Lord and encouraged by the Holy Spirit, it increased in numbers."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"🔎 Did you know? Without Barnabas, Saul might never have been accepted by the church, and we might never have had Paul's letters, which make up almost half the New Testament! One person's encouragement can change history."}],"lesson":{"title":"Be someone's Barnabas","text":"Everyone else saw Saul's past. Barnabas saw what God was doing in him, took a risk, and stood beside him. That one act of encouragement changed the world. Look for the person nobody trusts or includes, and be their Barnabas. Leaders believe in people."},"order":["Saul comes to Jerusalem","The disciples are afraid of him","They think it's a trick","Barnabas brings him to the apostles","Barnabas vouches for him","Saul speaks boldly, and the church grows"],"quiz":[{"q":"Why didn't the disciples trust Saul?","o":["They were afraid it was a trick","He was rude","He was a fisherman","He was too young"],"why":"Acts 9:26."},{"q":"Who stood up for Saul?","o":["Barnabas","Peter","James","Stephen"],"why":"Acts 9:27."},{"q":"What happened to the church afterwards?","o":["It enjoyed peace and grew","It shrank","It closed","Nothing"],"why":"Acts 9:31."}],"words":["BARNABAS","TRUST","ENCOURAGE","RISK","BELIEVE","INCLUDE"]},"ac13":{"passage":[[9,36,43]],"intro":[{"sc":"hut","n":"In the seaside town of Joppa there was a disciple named Tabitha (in Greek, Dorcas). She was always doing good and helping the poor."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"But she became sick and died. Her body was washed and placed in an upstairs room. The disciples heard Peter was nearby, and sent two men to urge him: \"Please come at once!\""},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"When Peter arrived, he was taken upstairs. All the widows stood around him, crying."},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"bwidowj","e":"worried","t":"Look, Peter, look at these coats and clothes Dorcas made for us. She made them while she was with us."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"Peter sent them all out of the room. Then he got down on his knees and prayed. Turning towards the dead woman, he said, \"Tabitha, get up.\""},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"bdorcas","e":"shock","t":"...Peter?"},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"She opened her eyes, and seeing Peter, she sat up! He took her by the hand and helped her to her feet. Then he called the believers, especially the widows, and presented her to them alive. This became known all over Joppa, and many people believed in the Lord."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"🔎 Did you know? 'Tabitha, get up' (Tabitha koum) sounds almost exactly like 'Talitha koum', what Jesus said to Jairus's daughter. Peter had been in that room with Jesus. He did just what he'd seen his Master do!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Small kindnesses leave a big mark","text":"Dorcas didn't preach sermons. She sewed clothes for widows. But when she died, everyone wept and held up the coats she'd made. Her quiet, practical kindness was a powerful ministry. Leaders serve with whatever skills they have: sewing, cooking, building, fixing."},"order":["Dorcas is always doing good","She becomes sick and dies","The disciples send for Peter","The widows show the clothes she made","\"Tabitha, get up\"","She sits up, and many believe"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Dorcas make for the widows?","o":["Coats and clothes","Bread","Pots","Baskets"],"why":"Acts 9:39."},{"q":"What did Peter do before speaking to her?","o":["Knelt and prayed","Sang","Left the room","Called a doctor"],"why":"Acts 9:40."},{"q":"What happened in Joppa afterwards?","o":["Many people believed in the Lord","Nothing","A storm came","Peter left at once"],"why":"Acts 9:42."}],"words":["DORCAS","TABITHA","CLOTHES","KINDNESS","WIDOWS","GETUP"]},"ac14":{"passage":[[10,9,23]],"intro":[{"sc":"rooftopsheet","n":"About noon, Peter went up on the flat roof of a house in Joppa to pray. He became hungry and wanted something to eat. While the meal was being prepared, he fell into a trance."},{"sc":"rooftopsheet","n":"He saw heaven opened and something like a large sheet being let down to earth by its four corners. It contained all kinds of animals, reptiles and birds, including ones the law of Moses said Jews must never eat."},{"sc":"rooftopsheet","n":"A voice said, \"Get up, Peter. Kill and eat.\""},{"sc":"rooftopsheet","w":"bpeter","e":"shock","t":"Surely not, Lord! I have never eaten anything impure or unclean!"},{"sc":"rooftopsheet","n":"The voice spoke a second time: \"Do not call anything impure that God has made clean.\" This happened three times, and then the sheet was taken back to heaven."},{"sc":"rooftopsheet","n":"While Peter was wondering what it meant, three men sent by a Roman centurion named Cornelius arrived at the gate, asking for him. The Spirit said, \"Go with them. Don't hesitate, for I have sent them.\""},{"sc":"rooftopsheet","n":"🔎 Did you know? For Jews, eating with non-Jewish people (Gentiles) or entering their homes was strictly avoided. God was about to show Peter that the vision wasn't really about food at all. It was about people!"}],"lesson":{"title":"God has no favourites","text":"Peter had grown up believing some people were 'unclean' and should be avoided. God used a strange vision to change Peter's thinking, just before sending him to visit a Roman soldier's home. Leaders let God challenge their prejudices about people who are different."},"order":["Peter prays on a roof at noon","He sees a sheet full of animals","\"Kill and eat\"","\"Surely not, Lord!\"","\"Don't call unclean what God has made clean\"","Three men arrive from Cornelius"],"quiz":[{"q":"Where was Peter praying?","o":["On a flat roof","In the temple","In a boat","In a cave"],"why":"Acts 10:9."},{"q":"What was in the sheet?","o":["All kinds of animals, reptiles and birds","Gold","Bread","Clothes"],"why":"Acts 10:12."},{"q":"How many times did the vision happen?","o":["Three","Once","Seven","Twice"],"why":"Acts 10:16."}],"words":["SHEET","VISION","ROOF","CLEAN","ANIMALS","PETER"]},"ac15":{"passage":[[10,24,28],[10,34,48]],"intro":[{"sc":"banquet","n":"Cornelius was a Roman centurion in Caesarea. He and his whole family loved God. He gave generously to people in need and prayed regularly. An angel had told him to send for Peter."},{"sc":"banquet","n":"When Peter arrived, Cornelius had gathered his relatives and close friends. He fell at Peter's feet. \"Stand up,\" Peter said, \"I'm only a man myself.\""},{"sc":"banquet","w":"bpeter","e":"smile","t":"You know it's against our law for a Jew to associate with a Gentile or visit one. But God has shown me that I should not call anyone impure or unclean."},{"sc":"banquet","w":"bpeter","e":"big","t":"I now realise how true it is that God does not show favouritism, but accepts from every nation the one who fears Him and does what is right."},{"sc":"banquet","n":"Peter told them about Jesus: His life, death and resurrection. While Peter was still speaking, the Holy Spirit came on all who heard the message, just as at Pentecost! They began speaking in tongues and praising God."},{"sc":"banquet","n":"Peter's Jewish companions were astonished: the Holy Spirit had been poured out even on Gentiles! So Peter ordered that they be baptised in the name of Jesus Christ."},{"sc":"banquet","n":"📜 Promise kept: God had promised Abraham, 'All nations on earth will be blessed through you' (Genesis 22:18). This was a turning point: the door to God's family was now wide open to every nation."}],"lesson":{"title":"Every nation, every tribe","text":"Peter learned that God doesn't have favourite nations, tribes or skin colours. A Roman soldier and his family received the Holy Spirit just like the first disciples. In God's family there's no 'us and them'. Leaders welcome people of every tribe and nation as equals."},"order":["Cornelius gathers his family and friends","Peter arrives at his house","\"God has shown me not to call anyone unclean\"","\"God does not show favouritism\"","The Holy Spirit falls on them all","They are baptised"],"quiz":[{"q":"Who was Cornelius?","o":["A Roman centurion","A fisherman","A priest","A king"],"why":"Acts 10:1."},{"q":"What did Peter realise about God?","o":["He does not show favouritism","He only loves Jews","He is angry","He is far away"],"why":"Acts 10:34."},{"q":"What happened while Peter was still speaking?","o":["The Holy Spirit came on all who heard","An earthquake","Everyone left","Nothing"],"why":"Acts 10:44."}],"words":["CORNELIUS","NATIONS","EQUAL","SPIRIT","GENTILES","WELCOME"]},"ac16":{"passage":[[11,19,26],[13,1,3]],"intro":[{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"Believers who had been scattered after Stephen's death travelled as far as Antioch, a huge city in Syria. Some of them, men from Cyprus and Cyrene (in Africa!), began to speak to Greeks too, telling them the good news about Jesus. A great number believed."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"The church in Jerusalem sent Barnabas to Antioch. When he arrived and saw what God's grace had done, he was glad, and encouraged them all. He was a good man, full of the Holy Spirit and faith."},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"Then Barnabas went to Tarsus to look for Saul. When he found him, he brought him to Antioch. For a whole year they taught great numbers of people."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"And the disciples were called 'Christians' first at Antioch! The name means 'Christ's people'."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"The leaders of the church in Antioch were a wonderfully mixed group: Barnabas from Cyprus; Simeon called Niger, which means 'black', probably from Africa; Lucius of Cyrene, from North Africa; Manaen, who had grown up with King Herod; and Saul."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"While they were worshipping and fasting, the Holy Spirit said, \"Set apart for Me Barnabas and Saul for the work to which I have called them.\" So after more fasting and prayer, they laid their hands on them and sent them off: the first missionary journey!"},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"🔎 Did you know? Two of the five leaders of the very first missionary-sending church were Africans! African believers helped send out Paul to the nations. Africa has been part of the church's leadership from the very beginning."}],"lesson":{"title":"A mixed team sends out missionaries","text":"The church in Antioch had leaders from Africa, Cyprus, the royal court and a former persecutor. That diverse team listened to the Holy Spirit together, and sent out the first missionaries. Leaders build teams from different backgrounds and send others out with prayer."},"order":["Scattered believers reach Antioch","Men from Cyprus and Cyrene preach to Greeks","Barnabas encourages the new church","Barnabas fetches Saul from Tarsus","Disciples are first called 'Christians'","The church sends Barnabas and Saul out"],"quiz":[{"q":"Where were the disciples first called Christians?","o":["Antioch","Jerusalem","Rome","Damascus"],"why":"Acts 11:26."},{"q":"Where was Lucius from?","o":["Cyrene, in North Africa","Rome","Greece","Egypt"],"why":"Acts 13:1."},{"q":"Who did the Holy Spirit set apart for mission?","o":["Barnabas and Saul","Peter and John","Simeon and Lucius","Philip and Stephen"],"why":"Acts 13:2."}],"words":["ANTIOCH","CHRISTIANS","CYRENE","NIGER","SENT","TEAM"]},"ac17":{"passage":[[12,1,17]],"intro":[{"sc":"prison","n":"King Herod (grandson of the Herod at Jesus' birth) began to persecute the church. He had James, the brother of John, put to death. When he saw this pleased the Jewish leaders, he arrested Peter too, planning to put him on trial after Passover."},{"sc":"prison","n":"Peter was kept in prison, chained between two soldiers, with sixteen soldiers guarding him. But the church was praying earnestly to God for him."},{"sc":"prison","n":"The night before his trial, Peter was sleeping! Suddenly an angel appeared and a light shone in the cell. He struck Peter on the side: \"Quick, get up!\" The chains fell off Peter's wrists. \"Put on your clothes and sandals, wrap your cloak around you and follow me.\""},{"sc":"prison","n":"Peter thought he was dreaming! They passed the first and second guards and came to the iron gate leading into the city. It opened for them by itself! Then the angel suddenly left him."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Peter went to the house of Mary, the mother of John Mark, where many people were praying. He knocked at the outer door, and a servant girl named Rhoda came to answer."},{"sc":"townnight","w":"brhoda","e":"big","t":"It's Peter! It's Peter's voice! He's at the door!"},{"sc":"townnight","n":"She was so overjoyed that she ran back without opening it! \"You're out of your mind!\" they told her. But she kept insisting. \"It must be his angel.\" But Peter kept on knocking! When they finally opened the door and saw him, they were astonished!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Expect God to answer","text":"The church was praying for Peter's release, and when God answered, they didn't believe it! They told Rhoda she was crazy. Rhoda, a young servant girl, was the one who believed first. Pray with faith, and don't be surprised when God answers. And sometimes the youngest have the strongest faith!"},"order":["Herod arrests Peter","The church prays earnestly","An angel wakes Peter","His chains fall off","The iron gate opens by itself","Rhoda leaves Peter knocking"],"quiz":[{"q":"How many soldiers guarded Peter?","o":["Sixteen","Two","One","A hundred"],"why":"Acts 12:4."},{"q":"What did Rhoda do when she heard Peter's voice?","o":["Ran to tell the others without opening the door","Opened the door","Screamed","Hid"],"why":"Acts 12:14."},{"q":"What did the people praying tell Rhoda?","o":["You're out of your mind!","Well done!","Go to sleep","Open it!"],"why":"Acts 12:15."}],"words":["RHODA","PRISON","ANGEL","CHAINS","KNOCKING","PRAYER"]},"ac18":{"passage":[[14,8,20]],"intro":[{"sc":"citygate","n":"In the town of Lystra sat a man who was lame from birth and had never walked. He listened to Paul speaking. Paul looked directly at him, saw that he had faith to be healed, and called out, \"Stand up on your feet!\" At that, the man jumped up and began to walk!"},{"sc":"citygate","n":"When the crowd saw this, they shouted in their own language: \"The gods have come down to us in human form!\" They called Barnabas 'Zeus' and Paul 'Hermes', because Paul did most of the talking!"},{"sc":"citygate","n":"The priest of Zeus brought bulls and flower wreaths to the city gates. He and the crowd wanted to offer sacrifices to them!"},{"sc":"citygate","w":"bpaul","e":"shock","t":"Friends, why are you doing this? We too are only human, like you! We're bringing you good news, telling you to turn from these worthless things to the living God, who made the heavens and the earth and the sea and everything in them."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"Even with these words, they could hardly stop the crowd from sacrificing to them."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"Then some enemies arrived from other cities and won the crowd over. They stoned Paul and dragged him outside the city, thinking he was dead. But after the disciples gathered around him, he got up and went back into the city!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Point people to God, not yourself","text":"The crowd wanted to worship Paul and Barnabas as gods! They could have enjoyed the fame. Instead, they tore their clothes and shouted, 'We're only human!' And the same crowd turned on them soon after. Leaders never accept praise that belongs to God, and don't trust the crowd's applause."},"order":["Paul heals a man lame from birth","The crowd calls them gods","They call Barnabas Zeus and Paul Hermes","The priest brings bulls for sacrifice","\"We are only human!\"","Paul is stoned, but gets up"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did the crowd call Barnabas?","o":["Zeus","Hermes","Apollo","King"],"why":"Acts 14:12."},{"q":"What did Paul shout?","o":["We are only human, like you!","Worship us!","Thank you!","Run!"],"why":"Acts 14:15."},{"q":"What happened to Paul afterwards?","o":["He was stoned but got up","He became king","He left on a ship","He was crowned"],"why":"Acts 14:19-20."}],"words":["LYSTRA","HUMAN","ZEUS","HERMES","HUMBLE","STONED"]},"ac19":{"passage":[[15,1,2],[15,6,11],[15,19,20],[15,36,41]],"intro":[{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"Some teachers came to Antioch saying, \"Unless non-Jewish believers follow all the Jewish customs of the law of Moses, they can't be saved.\" Paul and Barnabas strongly disagreed! So the church sent them to Jerusalem to discuss this huge question with the apostles and elders."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"After much discussion, Peter stood up: \"God, who knows the heart, gave the Holy Spirit to non-Jewish believers just as He did to us. He made no distinction between us and them. We believe it is through the grace of our Lord Jesus that we are saved, just as they are.\""},{"sc":"jerusalem","w":"bjamesj","e":"smile","t":"We should not make it difficult for the Gentiles who are turning to God. The words of the prophets agree: Amos said God would rebuild David's fallen tent, so that all the nations may seek the Lord."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"So they wrote a friendly letter to the new believers: they only asked them to avoid a few things that would make fellowship with Jewish believers hard. The new believers were overjoyed!"},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"Later, Paul and Barnabas planned a second journey. Barnabas wanted to take his cousin John Mark again. But Paul didn't, because Mark had left them halfway on the first journey. They had such a sharp disagreement that they parted company. Barnabas took Mark to Cyprus; Paul chose Silas."},{"sc":"jerusalem","n":"🔎 Did you know? The story has a happy ending! Years later, Paul wrote: 'Get Mark and bring him with you, because he is helpful to me' (2 Timothy 4:11). Barnabas's second chance for Mark paid off: Mark wrote the Gospel of Mark!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Disagree well","text":"The church faced a huge disagreement, and solved it by meeting, listening, looking at Scripture and agreeing together. Paul and Barnabas disagreed sharply too, and parted ways. But God used both teams, and later they were reconciled. Leaders disagree respectfully, and give people second chances."},"order":["Teachers say non-Jews must keep the law of Moses","Paul and Barnabas disagree","The church meets in Jerusalem","Peter: \"We are all saved by grace\"","James quotes Amos","Paul and Barnabas part over Mark"],"quiz":[{"q":"How did Peter say everyone is saved?","o":["Through the grace of the Lord Jesus","By keeping every law","By being Jewish","By being good"],"why":"Acts 15:11."},{"q":"Which prophet did James quote?","o":["Amos","Jonah","Daniel","Isaiah"],"why":"Acts 15:16-17; Amos 9:11."},{"q":"Why did Paul and Barnabas split up?","o":["They disagreed about taking Mark","They had a fight about money","One got sick","They never split"],"why":"Acts 15:37-39."}],"words":["GRACE","COUNCIL","DISAGREE","MARK","BARNABAS","SILAS"]},"ac20":{"passage":[[16,1,5]],"intro":[{"sc":"citygate","n":"Paul came to Derbe and then Lystra, the town where he'd been stoned. A disciple named Timothy lived there."},{"sc":"hut","n":"Timothy's mother, Eunice, was a Jewish believer, and his father was Greek. The believers in Lystra and Iconium spoke well of him."},{"sc":"hut","n":"Years later, Paul wrote to him: \"I remember your sincere faith, which first lived in your grandmother Lois and in your mother Eunice, and now, I am persuaded, lives in you also.\" Timothy had learned the Scriptures from his mum and grandma since he was a little child!"},{"sc":"hut","w":"bpaul","e":"smile","t":"Timothy, will you come with us on our journey?"},{"sc":"hut","w":"btimothy","e":"smile","t":"Yes, Paul! I'll come."},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"So Timothy joined Paul and Silas. As they travelled from town to town, the churches were strengthened in the faith and grew daily in numbers. Paul later called Timothy 'my true son in the faith'."},{"sc":"hut","n":"🔎 Did you know? Paul wrote two letters to Timothy, which are in the Bible: 1 and 2 Timothy. In them, he told him: 'Don't let anyone look down on you because you are young, but set an example for the believers in speech, in conduct, in love, in faith and in purity.'"}],"lesson":{"title":"Faith passed down","text":"Timothy's faith started with his grandmother and mother teaching him God's word at home. Then Paul invited him to join the team, young as he was. Leaders thank God for those who taught them, and young leaders set an example, without waiting to be older."},"order":["Paul visits Lystra again","Timothy has a good reputation","His grandmother Lois and mother Eunice taught him","Paul invites Timothy to join","Timothy travels with Paul and Silas","The churches grow stronger"],"quiz":[{"q":"Who taught Timothy the Scriptures as a child?","o":["His grandmother Lois and mother Eunice","Peter","His father","The priests"],"why":"2 Timothy 1:5; 3:15."},{"q":"Which town was Timothy from?","o":["Lystra","Rome","Jerusalem","Athens"],"why":"Acts 16:1."},{"q":"What did Paul tell Timothy about being young?","o":["Don't let anyone look down on you; set an example","Wait until you're older","Stay quiet","Go home"],"why":"1 Timothy 4:12."}],"words":["TIMOTHY","EUNICE","LOIS","YOUNG","EXAMPLE","FAITH"]},"ac21":{"passage":[[16,9,15]],"intro":[{"sc":"starsky","n":"During the night Paul had a vision of a man from Macedonia (in Europe) standing and begging him, \"Come over to Macedonia and help us!\""},{"sc":"shipstorm","n":"So 'we' got ready at once to leave for Macedonia. (Notice: Luke, the writer, starts saying 'we' here. He had joined the team!) They sailed across the sea to Europe, and came to Philippi, an important Roman city."},{"sc":"jordan","n":"On the Sabbath, they went outside the city gate to the river, expecting to find a place of prayer. They sat down and began to speak to the women who had gathered there."},{"sc":"jordan","n":"One of them was Lydia, a dealer in purple cloth, from the city of Thyatira. Purple dye was extremely expensive, so she was a successful businesswoman! She was a worshipper of God."},{"sc":"jordan","n":"\"The Lord opened her heart to respond to Paul's message.\" She and the members of her household were baptised."},{"sc":"jordan","w":"blydia","e":"smile","t":"If you consider me a believer in the Lord, come and stay at my house."},{"sc":"jordan","n":"And she persuaded them. Lydia became the first known Christian in Europe, and her home became the first church in Philippi!"}],"lesson":{"title":"God opens hearts","text":"Paul spoke, but it was God who 'opened Lydia's heart'. When we share about Jesus, we do our part, and God does the heart-work. And Lydia immediately used her home and resources for God. Leaders share faithfully, trust God to open hearts, and use what they have for His work."},"order":["Paul sees a man from Macedonia in a vision","\"Come and help us!\"","They sail to Philippi in Europe","They find women praying by the river","Lydia, a seller of purple cloth, listens","The Lord opens her heart"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Lydia sell?","o":["Purple cloth","Fish","Bread","Pots"],"why":"Acts 16:14."},{"q":"Where did Paul meet Lydia?","o":["By a river outside the city","In the temple","In prison","On a ship"],"why":"Acts 16:13."},{"q":"Who opened Lydia's heart?","o":["The Lord","Paul","Silas","Herself"],"why":"Acts 16:14."}],"words":["LYDIA","PURPLE","RIVER","PRAYER","EUROPE","HEART"]},"ac22":{"passage":[[16,22,34]],"intro":[{"sc":"market","n":"In Philippi, Paul and Silas were dragged before the city officials after Paul set a slave girl free from an evil spirit, ruining her owners' business. The crowd joined the attack."},{"sc":"prison","n":"They were stripped, beaten with rods and thrown into prison. The jailer put them in the inner cell and fastened their feet in wooden stocks."},{"sc":"prison","n":"About midnight, Paul and Silas were praying and singing hymns to God, and the other prisoners were listening to them!"},{"sc":"prison","n":"Suddenly there was such a violent earthquake that the foundations of the prison were shaken. At once all the prison doors flew open, and everyone's chains came loose!"},{"sc":"prison","n":"The jailer woke up, saw the prison doors open, and drew his sword to kill himself, because he thought the prisoners had escaped."},{"sc":"prison","w":"bpaul","e":"big","t":"Don't harm yourself! We are all here!"},{"sc":"prison","w":"bjailer","e":"worried","t":"Sirs, what must I do to be saved?"},{"sc":"prison","w":"bsilas","e":"smile","t":"Believe in the Lord Jesus, and you will be saved, you and your household."},{"sc":"hut","n":"That very hour of the night, the jailer washed their wounds; then he and all his household were baptised. He brought them into his house, set a meal before them, and was filled with joy, because he and his whole household had come to believe in God."}],"lesson":{"title":"Praise in the dark","text":"Beaten, bleeding, chained in the dark, Paul and Silas sang! The other prisoners were listening. Then, when they could have escaped, they stayed to save the jailer's life. Your attitude in hard times is a powerful witness. Leaders praise God in dark times, and care for others even when they're suffering."},"order":["Paul and Silas are beaten and jailed","Their feet are put in stocks","At midnight they sing hymns","An earthquake opens every door","\"We are all here!\"","The jailer and his family believe"],"quiz":[{"q":"What were Paul and Silas doing at midnight?","o":["Praying and singing hymns","Sleeping","Escaping","Crying"],"why":"Acts 16:25."},{"q":"What did the earthquake do?","o":["Opened the doors and loosened the chains","Destroyed the city","Nothing","Woke the city"],"why":"Acts 16:26."},{"q":"What did the jailer ask?","o":["What must I do to be saved?","Where are you going?","Who are you?","Why are you singing?"],"why":"Acts 16:30."}],"words":["MIDNIGHT","SINGING","EARTHQUAKE","JAILER","SAVED","CHAINS"]},"ac23":{"passage":[[17,10,12],[17,22,34]],"intro":[{"sc":"synagogue","n":"In the town of Berea, the people were more noble than those in Thessalonica. They received the message with great eagerness, and examined the Scriptures every day to see if what Paul said was true! Many of them believed."},{"sc":"athens","n":"Then Paul went to Athens, the most famous city of learning in the world, home of great philosophers. He was distressed to see that the city was full of idols."},{"sc":"athens","n":"The thinkers of Athens brought him to a meeting at the Areopagus, a famous hill: \"May we know what this new teaching is?\""},{"sc":"athens","w":"bpaul","e":"smile","t":"People of Athens! I see that you are very religious. As I walked around, I even found an altar with this inscription: TO AN UNKNOWN GOD. So you are worshipping something you don't know. Now what you worship as something unknown, I am going to tell you about!"},{"sc":"athens","w":"bpaul","e":"smile","t":"The God who made the world and everything in it is the Lord of heaven and earth. He doesn't live in temples built by human hands. From one man He made all the nations. He is not far from any one of us, for in Him we live and move and have our being!"},{"sc":"athens","n":"When Paul spoke about Jesus being raised from the dead, some of them laughed. Others said, \"We want to hear you again on this subject.\" And a few believed, including a council member named Dionysius and a woman named Damaris."},{"sc":"athens","n":"🔎 Did you know? Paul started where his listeners were: he quoted their own poets and used their altar to an 'unknown God' as a bridge to talk about Jesus. Good communicators connect with what people already know."}],"lesson":{"title":"Check, and connect","text":"The Bereans didn't just believe whatever they heard; they checked it against the Bible every day. And in Athens, Paul connected with people's own culture before pointing them to Jesus. Leaders check everything against Scripture, and find bridges to share the good news with people from every culture."},"order":["The Bereans check the Scriptures daily","Paul goes to Athens","The city is full of idols","\"An altar to an unknown God\"","\"In Him we live and move\"","Some laugh, some believe"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did the Bereans do every day?","o":["Examined the Scriptures","Built idols","Argued","Slept"],"why":"Acts 17:11."},{"q":"What was written on the altar in Athens?","o":["To an unknown God","To Zeus","To Paul","To Caesar"],"why":"Acts 17:23."},{"q":"What did Paul say God made all nations from?","o":["One man","Dust only","The sea","Many people"],"why":"Acts 17:26."}],"words":["BEREA","ATHENS","UNKNOWN","SCRIPTURES","CHECK","ALTAR"]},"ac24":{"passage":[[18,1,4],[18,24,28]],"intro":[{"sc":"market","n":"In Corinth, Paul met a Jewish man named Aquila and his wife Priscilla. They had recently left Rome because the emperor Claudius had ordered all Jews to leave."},{"sc":"market","n":"Paul went to see them, and because he was a tentmaker, as they were, he stayed and worked with them! Every Sabbath he reasoned in the synagogue."},{"sc":"market","w":"bpriscilla","e":"smile","t":"Paul, you're welcome to stay and work with us as long as you like!"},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"Later, a Jew named Apollos, a native of Alexandria in Egypt, came to Ephesus. He was a learned man, with a thorough knowledge of the Scriptures. He spoke with great fervour and taught about Jesus accurately, though he only knew about John's baptism."},{"sc":"synagogue","w":"bapollos","e":"big","t":"Jesus is the promised Messiah! Every Scripture points to Him!"},{"sc":"hut","n":"When Priscilla and Aquila heard him, they invited him to their home and explained to him the way of God more adequately. They didn't correct him in public; they took him aside kindly."},{"sc":"market","n":"Apollos humbly listened and learned, and went on to be a great help to the believers, proving from the Scriptures that Jesus was the Messiah."},{"sc":"market","n":"🔎 Did you know? Alexandria, in Egypt, was one of the greatest centres of learning in the ancient world, with a famous library. Apollos is one of several Africans who helped build the early church."}],"lesson":{"title":"Teach kindly, learn humbly","text":"Priscilla and Aquila saw that Apollos was missing something. They didn't embarrass him publicly; they invited him home and explained gently. And Apollos, a famous, brilliant speaker, was humble enough to learn. Leaders correct kindly in private, and stay teachable, however gifted they are."},"order":["Paul meets Priscilla and Aquila in Corinth","They are tentmakers like Paul","Apollos from Alexandria arrives","He speaks powerfully about Jesus","Priscilla and Aquila take him aside","Apollos learns, and helps many"],"quiz":[{"q":"What job did Paul, Priscilla and Aquila share?","o":["Tentmaking","Fishing","Farming","Carpentry"],"why":"Acts 18:3."},{"q":"Where was Apollos from?","o":["Alexandria in Egypt","Rome","Athens","Jerusalem"],"why":"Acts 18:24."},{"q":"How did Priscilla and Aquila help Apollos?","o":["Invited him home and explained privately","Corrected him publicly","Sent him away","Ignored him"],"why":"Acts 18:26."}],"words":["PRISCILLA","AQUILA","TENTS","APOLLOS","ALEXANDRIA","HUMBLE"]},"ac25":{"passage":[[19,18,20],[19,23,41]],"intro":[{"sc":"market","n":"In Ephesus, so many people turned to Jesus that those who had practised magic brought their scrolls together and burned them publicly. Their value was fifty thousand pieces of silver! \"In this way the word of the Lord spread widely and grew in power.\""},{"sc":"market","n":"Ephesus was famous for its huge temple to the goddess Artemis. A silversmith named Demetrius made silver models of the temple, and he made a fortune selling them."},{"sc":"market","w":"bdemetrius","e":"frown","t":"Men, you know we get our wealth from this business. But this fellow Paul has convinced large numbers of people that gods made by human hands are no gods at all! Our trade will lose its good name, and the temple of the great goddess Artemis will be discredited!"},{"sc":"theatre","n":"The craftsmen were furious and began shouting, \"Great is Artemis of the Ephesians!\" Soon the whole city was in an uproar. The crowd rushed into the huge theatre, dragging two of Paul's companions."},{"sc":"theatre","n":"The crowd was in confusion: some shouting one thing, some another. Most of the people didn't even know why they were there! For about two hours they shouted, \"Great is Artemis of the Ephesians!\""},{"sc":"theatre","n":"Finally the city clerk quietened them: \"These men haven't robbed temples or insulted our goddess. If Demetrius has a complaint, the courts are open. We're in danger of being charged with rioting!\" And he dismissed the crowd."},{"sc":"theatre","n":"🔎 Did you know? The theatre in Ephesus could hold about 25,000 people, and you can still visit its ruins today! The riot shows how much the good news was changing the city: even the idol-makers' businesses were affected."}],"lesson":{"title":"Don't follow the crowd","text":"Thousands of people shouted for two hours, and most didn't even know why they were there! Demetrius stirred them up because he was worried about money, not truth. Leaders think for themselves, ask 'why?', and don't get swept along by angry crowds."},"order":["People burn their magic scrolls","Demetrius makes silver shrines","He fears losing business","The city riots","The crowd fills the theatre","The city clerk calms them down"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Demetrius make?","o":["Silver models of Artemis's temple","Tents","Pots","Swords"],"why":"Acts 19:24."},{"q":"What did the crowd shout?","o":["Great is Artemis of the Ephesians!","Hosanna!","Crucify him!","Long live Caesar!"],"why":"Acts 19:28."},{"q":"What did most of the crowd not know?","o":["Why they were there","Where they were","Who Paul was","What day it was"],"why":"Acts 19:32."}],"words":["EPHESUS","RIOT","THEATRE","ARTEMIS","SILVER","CROWD"]},"ac26":{"passage":[[20,7,12]],"intro":[{"sc":"upperroom","n":"On the first day of the week, the believers in Troas came together to break bread. Paul was leaving the next day, so he kept on talking until midnight!"},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"They were meeting in an upstairs room on the third floor, with many lamps burning. It was getting hot and stuffy."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"Seated in a window was a young man named Eutychus. As Paul talked on and on, Eutychus sank into a deep sleep..."},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"beutychus","e":"worried","t":"Zzz..."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"...and fell out of the window, three storeys down to the ground! When they picked him up, he was dead."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"Paul went down, threw himself on the young man and put his arms around him. \"Don't be alarmed. He's alive!\""},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"Then Paul went back upstairs, broke bread, ate, and kept on talking until daylight! The people took the young man home alive and were greatly comforted."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"🔎 Did you know? 'Eutychus' means 'lucky'! Many preachers like to joke about this story: it's the Bible's warning about long sermons. But it also shows God's care for a tired young person."}],"lesson":{"title":"God cares about tired people too","text":"Eutychus wasn't being bad; it was late, hot and stuffy, and he was tired. When he fell, Paul didn't scold him. He ran down, hugged him, and God brought him back to life. Leaders are gentle with people who struggle, and maybe keep their speeches a bit shorter!"},"order":["Believers meet in Troas","Paul talks until midnight","Eutychus sits in a window","He falls asleep","He falls three storeys","Paul hugs him, and he's alive"],"quiz":[{"q":"What was the young man's name?","o":["Eutychus","Timothy","Mark","Silas"],"why":"Acts 20:9."},{"q":"Where was he sitting?","o":["In a window","On the floor","On the roof","At the door"],"why":"Acts 20:9."},{"q":"How long did Paul keep talking after that?","o":["Until daylight","Five minutes","He stopped","One hour"],"why":"Acts 20:11."}],"words":["EUTYCHUS","WINDOW","ASLEEP","MIDNIGHT","FELL","ALIVE"]},"ac27":{"passage":[[20,17,24],[20,32,38]],"intro":[{"sc":"galilee","n":"Paul was hurrying to reach Jerusalem. At the port of Miletus, he sent for the elders of the church in Ephesus, where he had spent three years."},{"sc":"galilee","w":"bpaul","e":"smile","t":"You know how I lived the whole time I was with you. I served the Lord with great humility and with tears. I didn't hesitate to tell you anything that would be helpful to you."},{"sc":"galilee","w":"bpaul","e":"worried","t":"Now, compelled by the Spirit, I'm going to Jerusalem, not knowing what will happen to me there. I only know that prison and hardships are facing me. But I consider my life worth nothing to me; my only aim is to finish the race and complete the task the Lord Jesus has given me."},{"sc":"galilee","w":"bpaul","e":"smile","t":"In everything I did, I showed you that by hard work we must help the weak, remembering the words the Lord Jesus Himself said: 'It is more blessed to give than to receive.'"},{"sc":"galilee","n":"When Paul had said this, he knelt down with all of them and prayed. They all wept as they embraced him and kissed him. What grieved them most was his statement that they would never see his face again. Then they walked with him to the ship."},{"sc":"galilee","n":"🔎 Did you know? 'It is more blessed to give than to receive' is a saying of Jesus that isn't written in any of the four Gospels! Paul remembered it, and it's only recorded here."}],"lesson":{"title":"Finish the race well","text":"Paul didn't know exactly what lay ahead, but he knew his goal: to finish the race God gave him. He'd led with humility, tears, hard work and generosity. The people loved him so much they wept to say goodbye. Leaders aim to finish well, and lead in a way people will miss."},"order":["Paul calls the Ephesian elders","\"I served the Lord with humility and tears\"","\"I'm going to Jerusalem\"","\"I want to finish the race\"","\"It is more blessed to give\"","They kneel, pray and weep"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Paul say was his only aim?","o":["To finish the race God gave him","To be rich","To go home","To rest"],"why":"Acts 20:24."},{"q":"Which words of Jesus did Paul quote?","o":["It is more blessed to give than to receive","Love your enemies","Follow Me","I am the way"],"why":"Acts 20:35."},{"q":"What did they do at the end?","o":["Knelt, prayed and wept","Had a party","Argued","Sang loudly"],"why":"Acts 20:36-37."}],"words":["GOODBYE","RACE","FINISH","GIVE","HUMILITY","TEARS"]},"ac28":{"passage":[[23,11,24]],"intro":[{"sc":"prison","n":"In Jerusalem, Paul was arrested after a riot in the temple courts, and held in the Roman barracks. The night after a stormy hearing, the Lord stood near Paul: \"Take courage! As you have testified about Me in Jerusalem, so you must also testify in Rome.\""},{"sc":"townnight","n":"The next morning, more than forty men formed a plot. They swore an oath not to eat or drink until they had killed Paul! They planned to ask for Paul to be brought to the council, and ambush him on the way."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"But the son of Paul's sister heard about this plot!"},{"sc":"prison","w":"bnephew","e":"worried","t":"Uncle Paul! I heard men plotting! Forty of them have sworn not to eat until they've killed you!"},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"Paul called a centurion: \"Take this young man to the commander; he has something to tell him.\" The commander took the young man by the hand, drew him aside and asked, \"What is it you want to tell me?\""},{"sc":"praetorium","w":"bnephew","e":"worried","t":"Forty men are waiting in ambush to kill Paul. They're ready now. Please don't give in to them!"},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"The commander dismissed the young man: \"Don't tell anyone you've reported this to me.\" That very night, he sent Paul away to Caesarea under the protection of 470 soldiers, horsemen and spearmen!"},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"🔎 Did you know? This is the only time Paul's nephew appears in the Bible, and we don't even know his name! But he was brave enough to walk into a Roman barracks and speak to the commander. A young person saved the greatest missionary's life."}],"lesson":{"title":"Young people can be brave","text":"Paul's nephew could have kept quiet. Instead, he went into the Roman barracks and told the commander, and saved his uncle's life. God used a young person whose name we don't even know. Leaders speak up when they know something is wrong, whatever their age."},"order":["The Lord says, \"Take courage\"","Forty men plot to kill Paul","Paul's nephew hears about it","He tells Paul","He tells the Roman commander","Paul is sent away with 470 soldiers"],"quiz":[{"q":"How many men plotted to kill Paul?","o":["More than forty","Two","Twelve","Seven"],"why":"Acts 23:13."},{"q":"Who discovered the plot?","o":["Paul's nephew","Luke","Timothy","A soldier"],"why":"Acts 23:16."},{"q":"How many soldiers protected Paul?","o":["470","10","1,000","None"],"why":"Acts 23:23."}],"words":["NEPHEW","PLOT","BRAVE","COMMANDER","COURAGE","YOUNG"]},"ac29":{"passage":[[26,12,20],[26,24,29]],"intro":[{"sc":"praetorium","n":"Paul spent two years as a prisoner in Caesarea. Then King Agrippa and his sister Bernice came, with great pomp, and Paul was brought before them."},{"sc":"praetorium","w":"bpaul","e":"smile","t":"King Agrippa, I consider myself fortunate to stand before you today. About noon, on the road to Damascus, I saw a light from heaven, brighter than the sun..."},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"Paul told his whole story: how he had persecuted Christians, met Jesus, and been sent to open people's eyes and turn them from darkness to light."},{"sc":"praetorium","w":"bpaul","e":"smile","t":"King Agrippa, do you believe the prophets? I know you do."},{"sc":"praetorium","w":"bagrippa","e":"smirk","t":"Do you think that in such a short time you can persuade me to be a Christian?"},{"sc":"praetorium","w":"bpaul","e":"big","t":"Short time or long, I pray to God that not only you, but all who are listening to me today may become what I am, except for these chains!"},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"Agrippa told the governor: \"This man could have been set free if he had not appealed to Caesar.\" Because Paul had asked to be tried by the emperor himself, he would be sent to Rome."},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"🔎 Did you know? The King James Version translates Agrippa's words as 'Almost thou persuadest me to be a Christian.' Many hymns and sermons have been written about being 'almost persuaded'. Almost isn't enough!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Your story is powerful","text":"Paul stood in chains before a king, and simply told his story: what he was like, how he met Jesus, and what changed. Then he invited the king to believe. Your own story of what God has done is one of your most powerful tools. Leaders share their story boldly, even before important people."},"order":["Paul is brought before King Agrippa","He tells about the light on the road","Jesus sent him to open people's eyes","\"Do you believe the prophets?\"","\"Can you persuade me so quickly?\"","\"I pray all of you become what I am\""],"quiz":[{"q":"Who did Paul speak to in this story?","o":["King Agrippa","Pharaoh","Herod the Great","Caesar"],"why":"Acts 26:1."},{"q":"What did Agrippa say?","o":["Do you think you can persuade me so quickly to be a Christian?","I believe!","Go away","Set him free"],"why":"Acts 26:28."},{"q":"Why was Paul sent to Rome?","o":["He had appealed to Caesar","He wanted a holiday","He was banished","He escaped"],"why":"Acts 26:32."}],"words":["AGRIPPA","STORY","CHAINS","PERSUADE","ALMOST","KING"]},"ac30":{"passage":[[27,13,26],[27,39,44]],"intro":[{"sc":"shipstorm","n":"Paul was put on a ship to Rome under a centurion named Julius. Paul warned them it was too late in the year to sail, but they didn't listen."},{"sc":"shipstorm","n":"Soon a wind of hurricane force, called the 'Northeaster', swept down. The ship was caught by the storm and couldn't head into the wind, so they gave way to it and were driven along. They threw the cargo overboard, then the ship's tackle."},{"sc":"shipstorm","n":"For many days neither sun nor stars appeared, and the storm kept raging. They finally gave up all hope of being saved."},{"sc":"shipstorm","w":"bpaul","e":"smile","t":"Men, keep up your courage! Last night an angel of the God to whom I belong and whom I serve stood beside me and said, 'Don't be afraid, Paul. God has graciously given you the lives of all who sail with you.' Not one of you will be lost; only the ship will be destroyed."},{"sc":"shipstorm","n":"On the fourteenth night, they sensed land. Paul urged everyone to eat something. He took bread, gave thanks to God in front of them all, broke it, and began to eat. They were all encouraged and ate too. There were 276 people on board."},{"sc":"shipstorm","n":"At daylight, they tried to run the ship onto a beach, but it struck a sandbar and the stern was broken to pieces by the waves. The soldiers planned to kill the prisoners, but Julius wanted to spare Paul's life and stopped them."},{"sc":"shipstorm","n":"He ordered those who could swim to jump overboard first. The rest got there on planks or pieces of the ship. And everyone reached land safely, all 276!"},{"sc":"shipstorm","n":"🔎 Did you know? Luke was on this ship! In this chapter he writes 'we' and gives amazing sailing details. Historians say it's one of the most accurate descriptions of an ancient sea voyage ever written."}],"lesson":{"title":"Calm in the storm","text":"A prisoner in chains became the leader on a sinking ship! While soldiers and sailors panicked, Paul trusted God's promise, encouraged everyone, gave thanks for bread, and got them to eat. Everyone survived. Leaders stay calm in crises, encourage others, and trust God's promises."},"order":["Paul warns them not to sail","A hurricane-force wind strikes","They give up all hope","\"Keep up your courage!\"","Paul gives thanks for bread","All 276 people reach land safely"],"quiz":[{"q":"How many people were on board?","o":["276","12","1,000","50"],"why":"Acts 27:37."},{"q":"What did Paul tell everyone?","o":["Keep up your courage, no one will be lost","We're doomed","Jump now","Pray to the sea"],"why":"Acts 27:22."},{"q":"How did those who couldn't swim reach land?","o":["On planks and pieces of the ship","In a lifeboat","They didn't","On a whale"],"why":"Acts 27:44."}],"words":["SHIPWRECK","STORM","COURAGE","SAILORS","PLANKS","SAFE"]},"ac31":{"passage":[[28,1,10]],"intro":[{"sc":"beachfire","n":"Once safely on shore, they found out the island was called Malta. The islanders showed them unusual kindness. They built a fire and welcomed everyone, because it was raining and cold."},{"sc":"beachfire","n":"Paul gathered a pile of brushwood, and as he put it on the fire, a viper, driven out by the heat, fastened itself on his hand!"},{"sc":"beachfire","n":"When the islanders saw the snake hanging from his hand, they said to each other, \"This man must be a murderer! Though he escaped from the sea, justice has not allowed him to live!\""},{"sc":"beachfire","n":"But Paul shook the snake off into the fire and suffered no ill effects."},{"sc":"beachfire","n":"The people expected him to swell up or suddenly fall dead. But after waiting a long time and seeing nothing unusual happen to him, they changed their minds and said he was a god!"},{"sc":"hut","n":"Publius, the chief official of the island, welcomed them into his home. His father was sick in bed with fever and dysentery. Paul went in, prayed, placed his hands on him and healed him. Then the rest of the sick on the island came and were cured."},{"sc":"beachfire","n":"🔎 Did you know? First the islanders thought Paul was a murderer; then they thought he was a god! Paul was neither. People's opinions can swing wildly. What matters is what God says about you."}],"lesson":{"title":"Shake it off","text":"After a shipwreck, a snake bite! Paul simply shook it off into the fire and carried on. Then he served the island by praying for the sick. When bad things happen and people misjudge you, shake it off, trust God, and keep serving. Leaders don't let setbacks or other people's opinions stop them."},"order":["The islanders of Malta show kindness","They build a fire in the rain","A viper bites Paul's hand","\"He must be a murderer!\"","Paul shakes it off into the fire","Paul heals the sick on the island"],"quiz":[{"q":"What island did they land on?","o":["Malta","Crete","Cyprus","Sicily"],"why":"Acts 28:1."},{"q":"What bit Paul?","o":["A viper","A dog","A scorpion","A shark"],"why":"Acts 28:3."},{"q":"What did Paul do with the snake?","o":["Shook it off into the fire","Ran away","Kept it","Threw it at someone"],"why":"Acts 28:5."}],"words":["MALTA","VIPER","FIRE","SHAKE","KINDNESS","HEALED"]},"ac32":{"passage":[[28,14,16],[28,30,31]],"intro":[{"sc":"rome","n":"And so they came to Rome, the capital of the whole empire! Believers from Rome travelled out to meet Paul on the road. At the sight of them, Paul thanked God and was encouraged."},{"sc":"rome","n":"In Rome, Paul was allowed to live by himself, with a soldier to guard him."},{"sc":"rome","n":"For two whole years Paul stayed there in his own rented house, chained to a guard, and welcomed all who came to see him."},{"sc":"rome","w":"bpaul","e":"big","t":"Come in, come in! Let me tell you about the kingdom of God, and about the Lord Jesus Christ!"},{"sc":"rome","n":"He proclaimed the kingdom of God and taught about the Lord Jesus Christ, with all boldness, and without hindrance!"},{"sc":"rome","n":"And that's how the book of Acts ends: not with a full stop, but with the good news still spreading, 'unhindered'. During these years, Paul also wrote letters that are in our Bibles: Ephesians, Philippians, Colossians and Philemon."},{"sc":"rome","n":"🔎 Did you know? Why does Acts end so suddenly? Some think it's because the story isn't finished. The good news is still spreading, from Jerusalem to Rome, to Africa, to Nigeria, to your town, to you. YOU are part of Acts chapter 29!"}],"lesson":{"title":"The story continues with you","text":"Jesus said, 'You will be My witnesses to the ends of the earth.' Acts shows the good news spreading from 120 people in a room to the capital of the world. Paul was chained, but God's word wasn't. The story isn't finished. Leaders carry it on, boldly, wherever God places them."},"order":["Believers meet Paul on the road","Paul arrives in Rome","He lives in a rented house with a guard","He welcomes everyone who comes","He preaches boldly for two years","The story continues with us"],"quiz":[{"q":"Where does the book of Acts end?","o":["Rome","Jerusalem","Athens","Malta"],"why":"Acts 28:16."},{"q":"How long did Paul stay in his rented house?","o":["Two years","Two days","Ten years","A month"],"why":"Acts 28:30."},{"q":"How did Paul preach in Rome?","o":["Boldly and without hindrance","Secretly","He didn't","Only to soldiers"],"why":"Acts 28:31."}],"words":["ROME","BOLD","UNHINDERED","KINGDOM","WITNESS","CONTINUE"]}});
